    not_duplicate_of: []  # b5c5
    pr_ref:  # b5c5
    description: "The dependency-linker builds a global flat dict[dep_name -> Symbol], so when a dependency name is declared in more than one package's manifest, only the last-written manifest symbol survives; depends_on_manifest edges from importing files in OTHER packages are linked to that wrong manifest, ignoring the importing file's own package. All 26 depends_on_manifest edges in the substrate point to hypergumbo-tracker/pyproject.toml. 3 of them originate in hypergumbo-core source files importing rich (cli.py, sketch.py, tests/test_sketch.py) but are linked to toml:packages/hypergumbo-tracker/pyproject.toml:24-24:rich:dependency even though hypergumbo-core's own rich dependency node exists. 6 dep names are declared in >1 package (rich, pygments, pyyaml, hypergumbo-core, hypergumbo-lang-mainstream, tree-sitter-language-pack). 3/26 edges provably misattributed; the other 23 are 'correct' only incidentally (tracker was last manifest written). Root cause (linkers/dependency.py): _build_dependency_lookup (83-104) maps lookup[sym.name]=sym with NO package scoping (later same-named dep overwrites earlier); link_dependencies (137-169) does dep_lookup.get(root_pkg) with no consideration of which package edge.src lives in (code_symbols passed but 'reserved for future use'). Fresh repro: /tmp/depmanifest_test pkgA+pkgB each declaring+importing rich → both depends_on_manifest edges point to pkgA's manifest; pkgB's import linked to pkgA. Reproduces cleanly."  # b5c5
    fields: {}  # b5c5
